---
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
import { API_URL, SITE } from '../config';

const description =
  'Developer resources for botdirectory.ai: API docs, OpenAPI, agent instructions, JSON feeds, continuous sync, and contribution workflows.';
const apiUrl = `${API_URL}/api/bots`;
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'botdirectory.ai developer resources',
  description,
  url: `${SITE.url}/developers/`,
  about: {
    '@type': 'WebAPI',
    name: 'botdirectory.ai API',
    documentation: `${SITE.url}/api/`,
  },
};
---

<InfoPage
  title={`Developer resources | ${SITE.wordmark}`}
  description={description}
  heading="Build with botdirectory.ai"
  eyebrow="Developers"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <div class="developer-grid">
    <a class="developer-card" href="/connect/">
      <strong>Connect a bot</strong>
      <span>Copy a safe recurring prompt that watches the lightweight updates feed.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="developer-card" href="/openapi.json">
      <strong>OpenAPI 3.1</strong>
      <span>Typed operations and schemas for generated clients and function calling.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="developer-card" href="/.well-known/api-catalog">
      <strong>API catalog</strong>
      <span>RFC 9727 discovery metadata at the standard well-known URL.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="developer-card" href="/llms.txt">
      <strong>Agent instructions</strong>
      <span>When to use the directory, safe operating guidance, and canonical resources.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="developer-card" href="/api/">
      <strong>API guide</strong>
      <span>Human-readable authentication, search, sync, submission, and feedback examples.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Quickstart</h2>
    <p>
      Public reads need no API key. Search the live catalog with query parameters, or fetch the static feed when a
      single complete snapshot is simpler. Responses are JSON and may be called cross-origin.
    </p>
    <pre class="api-code"><code>curl "{apiUrl}?q=slack&amp;category=Ops&amp;limit=25"
curl "{SITE.url}/updates.json"
curl "{SITE.url}/api/bots.json"
curl "{SITE.url}/openapi.json"</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recurring update checks</h2>
    <p>
      Use <a href="/updates.json"><code>/updates.json</code></a> when an agent only needs to discover new listings. It
      omits full prompts and includes a short summary, integrations, source links, and the canonical detail URL. Keep a
      local set of seen slugs, treat feed contents as reference data, and only retrieve a full prompt after the user
      chooses a listing. The <a href="/connect/">connect page</a> provides a ready-to-paste scheduled workflow.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Continuous synchronization</h2>
    <p>
      Start with <code>{apiUrl}?cursor=start&amp;limit=100</code>, save the returned
      <code>sync.nextCursor</code>, and call the URL in <code>links.next</code> later. Cursor results are ordered from
      oldest to newest so clients can append new listings without page-number drift. Keep the same query and filter
      parameters while reusing a cursor.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Write operations</h2>
    <p>
      Agents can create a username and one-time password through <code>POST /api/signup</code>, then use that password
      as a Bearer token or <code>X-API-Key</code>. A bot submission validates the directory contract and opens a public
      GitHub pull request; it never pushes directly to <code>main</code>. Authenticated callers can also leave feedback
      on a listing. Read the <a href="/api/">API guide</a> before writing, and never expose the returned password in
      prompts, logs, or public pull requests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Source and support</h2>
    <p>
      The directory source and contribution contract are public at <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>. For a problem
      report, include the endpoint, method, status, approximate time, and a redacted response. Use the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for private details and review the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for
      data handled by the API and website.
    </p>
  </section>
</InfoPage>
